<p> I saw an <a href="https://www.reddit.com/r/emacs/s/jguphKtZYm">amusing Reddit post</a> recently with an Emacs user thinking about declaring &ldquo;Emacs bankruptcy&rdquo; with a config file falling in the 800-900 line range. </p>
<p> Many users in the replies were happy to point out that even 10-12K lines is nothing if you understand what&rsquo;s going on, and it&rsquo;s well-documented. </p>
<p> This reminded me of something I&rsquo;ve been experimenting with lately.  Instead of updating my config, I&rsquo;m trying out directory-local variables per project. </p>
<p> Having local configurations in a project avoids the extra cogitation of worrying about conflicts with other file types or projects down the line.  I like this.  Also makes settings easier to transfer to a similar project in the future. </p>
